      },
      "layout_tag": "section-title",
      "confidence": 0.8604913949966431,
      "reading_order": 5,
      "text": "3.1.1. Policy for Tourism Development in India"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260726_ee793a2d-3b21-491e-acf2-0bffa5f48f31_1_block_005",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 284.0,
        "y1": 786.0,
        "x2": 2196.0,
        "y2": 1117.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9505923986434937,
      "reading_order": 6,
      "text": "The Travel & Tourism sector holds strategic importance in the Indian economy providing substantial\nsocio-economic benefits. Moreover, through its direct economic impacts such as accommodation\nservices, food & beverage services, retail trade and transportation services, the sector has significant\nindirect and induced impacts such as travel & tourism investment, government collective travel &\ntourism investment and consumption of direct and indirect employees."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260726_ee793a2d-3b21-491e-acf2-0bffa5f48f31_1_block_006",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 283.0,
        "y1": 1161.0,
        "x2": 2194.0,
        "y2": 1425.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9452865719795227,
      "reading_order": 7,
      "text": "India has been witnessing steady growth in its travel and tourism sector over the past few years. The\ntotal contribution of Travel & Tourism to GDP in India was INR 8,309.4 billion (7.4% of GDP) in 2015,\nand was forecasted to rise to INR 8,913.6 billion (7.3% of GDP) in 2016, with 6.5% CAGR (Compound\nAverage Growth Rate) in the last seven years."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260726_ee793a2d-3b21-491e-acf2-0bffa5f48f31_1_block_007",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 650.0,
        "y1": 1498.0,
        "x2": 1861.0,
        "y2": 2225.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "chart",
      "confidence": 0.9689782857894897,
      "reading_order": 8,
      "text": "| Year | Direct Contribution (bil INR) | Indirect Contribution (bil INR) | Growth Rate (%) | Total Value (bil INR) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 2010 | ~1,950 | ~4,100 | ~6.7% | ~6,050 |\n| 2011 | ~2,050 | ~4,300 | ~5.2% | ~6,350 |\n| 2012 | ~2,150 | ~4,500 | ~6.8% | ~6,650 |\n| 2013 | ~2,250 | ~4,800 | ~6.4% | ~7,050 |\n| 2014 | ~2,450 | ~5,300 | ~9.3% | ~7,750 |\n| 2015 | ~2,650 | ~5,500 | ~7.2% | ~8,150 |\n| 2016E | ~2,800 | ~5,200 | ~7.9% | ~8,000 |"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260726_ee793a2d-3b21-491e-acf2-0bffa5f48f31_1_block_008",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 529.0,
