      "layout_tag": "image-caption",
      "confidence": 0.8435937166213989,
      "reading_order": 10,
      "text": "Figure 3.1.1 Travel & Tourism’s Contribution to GDP and Its Growth Rate"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260726_ee793a2d-3b21-491e-acf2-0bffa5f48f31_1_block_010",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 283.0,
        "y1": 2481.0,
        "x2": 2196.0,
        "y2": 2880.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9614061713218689,
      "reading_order": 11,
      "text": "This contribution share to GDP (7.4% in 2015) is relatively low compared to other countries in the\nAsia-Pacific region, such as 29.9% in Cambodia and 20.8% in Thailand. It is even below the world\naverage of 9.8% and Asia-Pacific average of 8.5%. The total contribution to employment in 2015\nshowed 8.7% in India, which is also below the world average of 9.5% and slightly higher than\nAsia-Pacific average of 8.6%. This shows the possibility that India’s Travel & Tourism sector can\nexpand its contribution to GDP."
    },
